    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d750">

                <pb facs="0781" n="773" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg773"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/655: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-25T19:00:00-04:00">August 25, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>476. For Taylor and Rublee. Your 753, August 12, 4 p.m. A preliminary report from
                        Norweb<anchor n="19" xml:id="d750-f1"/> states that, while the Dominican
                    Government <pb facs="0782" n="774" xml:id="pg774"/> is keenly anxious to secure
                    “easily assimilable neo-white” agricultural colonists from Porto Rico or other
                    nearby areas, the type of refugees for whom relief is sought, who come
                    principally from urban centers, is the type least desired by the Dominican
                    Government. He feels that the Dominican offer is simply a gesture and that it
                    should not be taken at its face value. A copy of his report is being forwarded
                    by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d750-f1" n="19" xml:id="d750-f1-content">
                <p>Despatch No. 416, August 20, from the Minister in the Dominican Republic, not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
